id: pm-vcs-phase6packs
title: Compact loose chunks into indexed pack storage
description: "The measured slice uses existing compressed loose objects. Design pack compaction with stable uncompressed identities, indexed ranges, reachability-aware retention, resumable publication and authorized erasure compatibility."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: "gh:unbraind/pm-vcs#150","gh:unbraind/pm-vcs#154","gh:unbraind/pm-vcs#158"
created_at: "2026-10-21T14:49:57.681Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T19:22:59.129Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Pack and loose representations retain the same logical identities; range reads and GC work across both; corruption and interrupted compaction fail safely.
parent: pm-vcs-b7cb
comments[148]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T00:35:13.935Z",codex-agent,"Design: indexed independently compressed object frames preserve uncompressed SHA-256 identities. Compaction, GC and authorized erasure share the existing ObjectStore writer lease; durable publication precedes loose retirement. Add mixed-storage differential, crash-boundary and competing-writer regressions in non-git trackers; benchmark a public tracker copy. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-25T00:50:06.625Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: bounded independently compressed indexed packs, actual physical member ranges in InventoryEntry, typed PackRefusal remedies, SDK ObjectStore.compact and vcs compact TOON/JSON counts. GC uses the complete existing retention-root walk; authorized erasure materializes verified loose copies and retires packs before the existing permanent-denial/deletion proof. Every transition reads under ObjectStore.withWriteLock and releases last; retries retire duplicate representations. Foreign staging records remain untouched with explicit skip reasons. SDK gap: the host ExtensionCommandSdk has no binary object-pack or compressed-range-storage primitive; binary storage reuses the package-owned store lease and filesystem backend."
  "2026-10-25T00:50:09.311Z",codex-agent,"Revert proofs: disabling only PackStorage.compact caused 18 new regressions to fail (3 unrelated validation/read tests still passed); bypassing only PackStorage.index validation made the malformed-index regression fail; restoring only the original ObjectStore.read made the peer-retirement retry regression fail; restoring only the original collectGarbage made its exhaustive crash schedule regression fail. All functions were restored immediately after each proof. Targeted existing ObjectStore/GC regressions passed 43/43; new storage and benchmark source reached 100% statements/lines/functions, with the final missing malformed-JSON branch now covered."
  "2026-10-25T00:53:16.802Z",codex-agent,"PM-linked targeted command passed 64/64 tests with zero skips, failures or cancellations, including real SIGKILL and competing-process schedules on one non-git tracker. Follow-up focused checks passed the foreign-record tolerance, real inventory ranges, all 48 command contracts, and bounded agent receipts. Additional revert proofs: removing only the 20-entry receipt cap failed its omission-count regression; restoring only the original collectGarbage failed the random-corpus differential test by losing live packed reads. Project test-result tracking is disabled by existing policy, so these measured results are recorded here rather than changing that setting."
  "2026-10-25T00:54:25.140Z",codex-agent,"Public real-data validation: read-only copy of the public unbraind/pm-vcs tracker at c7790d45aab22a3a28b4d44955a592dfc06e715e, 330 tracked files and 343 native objects in a non-git project. Loose: 343 files, 1357177 compressed bytes, 2187264 allocated bytes; pack: 1 file, 1262545 compressed bytes, 1265664 allocated bytes. Warm verified-read median/p95 (301 samples): loose 0.105721/0.894680 ms; packed 0.241476/1.440179 ms. All 686 differential reads across compaction and GC matched; GC removed 0 live objects. Packed reads are slower in this measurement; no speedup claim. Aggregate receipt: docs/indexed-pack-benchmark.json. Full npm/Bun release-gate evidence will come from CI because the shared host is saturated."
  "2026-10-25T00:59:33.858Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/150 . Final concurrency hardening rejects symlink-aliased object roots before staging recovery can touch a store protected by a different lexical lease path. The focused maintenance/foreign/output tests passed 3/3; disabling only the early root guard made the ownership-preservation regression fail (1 test, 1 failure), then restoration passed. Local typecheck, test typecheck and lint passed. The self-host writer/committed acceptance gate is repeated for this change and PM metadata. Full unchanged-threshold npm/Bun gates are running in PR CI; final exact-head counts and links will be published in the PR and handoff. Item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification; no merge or release."
  "2026-10-25T01:09:11.793Z",codex-agent,"CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/40148633317 measured all 83 production files at 100% statements, branches, functions and lines on Node 22 and 26. Its sole test failure was the explicit source-inventory assertion still declaring 80 files (1901/1902 tests passed); Bun was correctly not counted as evidence. Updated that declaration to 83 to include engine/packs.ts, engine/object-error.ts and scripts/pack-benchmark.ts, preserving every coverage threshold and ignore-directive guard. The focused raw-coverage tests pass after the inventory correction. Exact-head full npm/Bun gates will rerun after this committed self-host update."
  "2026-10-25T01:22:42.095Z",codex-agent,"Final foreign-record audit found an erasure gap: skipping a valid owned staging job as a whole when it contained a foreign child could retain the owned payload; recursive post-publication cleanup could also delete a late foreign child. Recovery/publication now remove only regular payload and owner leaves, in payload-first order, remove only empty directories, and report late foreign records with bounded skip details. New tests preserve foreign records injected at every staging cleanup boundary and prove authorized erasure removes the owned staging payload beside foreign notes. Focused tests passed 4/4 plus typecheck/test typecheck/lint. Revert proofs: restoring only the whole-job foreign skip fails the erasure regression (1/1 fails); restoring recursive cleanup fails both preservation/error regressions (2/2 fail). Expanded real SIGKILL/interleaving schedules now include each staging-leaf retirement boundary."
  "2026-10-25T01:27:23.162Z",codex-agent,"Expanded PM-linked targeted c8 command passed 26/26 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, and 100% statements/branches/functions/lines for engine/packs.ts and scripts/pack-benchmark.ts. This includes real SIGKILL and real competing compact transitions at every added staging payload/marker/directory retirement boundary. Late foreign-report deduplication uses a Set to remain linear; follow-up foreign/erasure/output/error checks passed 5/5 after that reporting refinement. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, duplication and docstring gates passed. Final source is frozen for exact-head CI npm/Bun release gates; the PM claim is released while status remains in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-25T03:30:22.151Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator review reopened implementation work on PR 150. Close the reader class with one generation-checked resolver and pinned descriptors for logical, typed, bounded, streaming, existence and inventory APIs; enumerate the exported reader surface and cover every reader against every compact/unpack/repack/GC boundary. Use an eight-attempt bounded retry and distinguish stable absence from active transitions. Centralize filesystem durability, exercise forced capabilities and real Windows GC, skip recognized loose temporaries before decoding, and record isolated read/durability revert proofs. Preserve completed pack identity, retention and benchmark evidence; keep the item in_progress."
  "2026-10-25T03:57:35.462Z",codex-agent,"Review follow-up: every logical reader now uses one generation resolver with a maximum of 8 attempts and pinned file/range handles. Enumerated 21 reader entry points. The writer-boundary matrix passed 5,670 live/erased checks across 135 compaction, unpack, repack and GC boundaries on one real non-git tracker; resolution interleavings also passed. Pack crash/concurrency regressions pass 27/27, durability plus erasure regressions pass 27/27. One platform-aware durability helper now owns all production fsync/rename/link/deletion operations; Windows CI additionally runs shipped CLI gc --apply. Recognized empty/truncated loose temporaries are skipped before decoding. Updated public-tracker benchmark verifies 686 reads of 343 objects: 343 loose files / 1,357,186 bytes / 2,187,264 allocated bytes versus 1 pack / 1,262,531 bytes / 1,265,664 allocated bytes; median/p95 milliseconds 0.243544/0.837920 loose and 0.393645/1.316102 packed (301 samples each, shared busy host)."
  "2026-10-25T03:57:37.221Z",codex-agent,"Isolated behavioural revert proof for reader class: disabled only the changed-generation retry branch in ObjectStore.resolveLocation, then ran node --test --test-name-pattern='retired pack catalog' test/object-read-protocol.test.ts. The retained-object lookup failed (0 pass, 1 fail, false presence after GC repacked survivors). Restoring the branch made the same command pass 1/1. Durability class: restored the unsupported-directory-fsync refusal only in durability.directory with capability forced off, then ran node --test --test-name-pattern='capability can be forced' test/durability.test.ts. It failed 0/1 with unsupported_durability; restoring the platform-aware helper passed 1/1. Neither revert was retained."
  "2026-10-25T04:01:53.563Z",codex-agent,"Additional revert proof: removed only the pre-decode recognized-temporary skip from ObjectStore.looseLocations and ran node --test --test-name-pattern='zero-byte and truncated' test/packs.test.ts. It failed 0/1 with corrupt_object; restoring the skip passed 1/1. Pinned descriptor ownership also fixes a worker double-close discovered by the existing feature-edge tests (23/23 passing). Typecheck, test compilation, lint, duplication and docstring gates pass at unchanged thresholds. The linked reader/durability command ran via pm test --run --only-last --progress and passed 10/10; result recording is disabled by project policy, so aggregate evidence is recorded here without changing policy. New targeted tests additionally cover corrupted/changing generation metadata, exhausted inventory retries, stable native I/O errors, retired inventory deduplication, descriptor truncation, and denial checks while physical bytes still exist."
  "2026-10-25T04:09:01.030Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up validation found and fixed two class-adjacent issues before final acceptance. Existing strace one-open assertions caught eager hydration reopening present objects; read, bounded reads, streams and default state now resolve once and hydrate only stable absence. Existing byte budgets remain unchanged and traces now include positioned pread64 reads. Six bounded-I/O cases pass, including a 128 MiB leaf corpus read once with bounded retained buffers; the upload-ordering case separately passes with explicit fail-closed logical-probe evidence when denial metadata is corrupt. Windows CI run 40160452176 exposed metadata fsync on a read-only handle (EPERM); writeAtomicJson now opens its flush handle writable. A portable real-filesystem Windows handle-contract regression passes. Reverting only that open mode fails 0/1 with EPERM and restoration passes 1/1. Reintroducing only eager hydration in read fails the existing shared-import one-open regression 0/1; restoration passes 1/1. Final benchmark after the one-open fix: 343 loose files / 1,357,188 compressed bytes / 2,187,264 allocated versus 1 pack / 1,262,537 compressed / 1,265,664 allocated; median/p95 ms 0.185120/0.636548 loose and 0.277932/1.413965 packed; 301 samples each, 686 verified comparisons, 0 live GC removals."
  "2026-10-25T04:18:05.989Z",codex-agent,"Complete exported-reader audit now includes SharedObjectStore's four overrides: 25 logical entry points total. The PM-linked reader/durability target passes 14/14 with 6,750 live/erased checks (25 readers x 135 writer boundaries x 2) and 700 resolver schedules (25 x 4 transitions x 7 boundaries), plus denied checks. Shared chunk streams retain missing_fragment remedies; reverting only that override fails the focused regression 0/1 and restoring it passes 1/1. Busy state inspection now propagates object_store_changing after exactly 8 attempts rather than falsely reporting corruption; reverting only this guard fails 0/1. Recognized loose temporary stream paths now resolve store authorization before decoding; reverting only this native-path recognition fails 0/1 by allowing a denied temporary payload. Both restored focused checks pass 2/2. Presence/type probes, pack backend error passthrough and inventory native errors are explicitly covered. Windows shipped-CLI GC passes on Node 22 and 26 in CI run 40160870184; npm/Bun full release gates are still running."
  "2026-10-25T04:26:18.584Z",codex-agent,"CI-driven final regression closure: central durability calls now preserve native filesystem hooks, so existing worktree race tests can inject real leaf replacement and directory-pruning races. The unchanged node --test test/worktree-races.test.ts suite passes 266/266 across four capability configurations. Reverting only unlink/rmdir dispatch in the durability helper to captured native functions fails the 12 focused competing-transition cases; restoring dynamic native dispatch passes all 12. Stream tests now cover a direct indexed-pack path and a descriptor denied before iteration, and remove obsolete worker-path ENOENT translation because workers read pinned descriptors. Targeted stream coverage is 100% in statements/branches/functions/lines with 10/10 cases. The manifest negative-marker test also includes unsupported version 99, preserving the format-corruption refusal branch. Full-gate thresholds and source inventory remain unchanged (84 production files)."
  "2026-10-25T05:05:38.629Z",codex-agent,"Full release evidence passed for code head 0a34c538db46b4fe3b38dc904f857ab8c96e0102: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/40162026200 . Node 22 and Node 26 each pass npm run release:check 1,922/1,922 and bun run release:check 1,922/1,922, plus native Bun 32/32. All four release gates report 100% statements, branches, functions and lines across all 84 production files, with zero failed, skipped or cancelled suite tests. Windows shipped CLI gc --apply passes 1/1 on each Node version; CodeQL passes. The 25-reader matrix covers 6,750 live/erased checks at 135 compaction/unpack/repack/GC boundaries plus 700 resolver schedules; bounded retry is 8. Stream and durability target coverage is 100% in all dimensions. Pack crash/concurrency suite passes 27/27, worktree races 266/266, focused PM-linked native races 12/12, and all requested isolated behavioural revert proofs are recorded above. Real-data receipt remains docs/indexed-pack-benchmark.json (343 objects, 686 comparisons). SDK gap remains the absence of a binary object-pack/compressed-range primitive in the pinned ExtensionCommandSdk; existing native lease/retention/erasure and host tracker/rendering APIs are reused. Local pinned-host pm health reports an installed pm-github 2026.10.24 versus host 2026.10.20 skew; CI health passes with its configured compatible extension. No dependency pin or existing history record was changed. Implementation complete; item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification. The claim is released while the final receipt-only commit is validated."
  "2026-10-25T05:18:31.529Z",codex-agent,"Final manual corruption audit found a reader-refactor regression despite the green full gate: the old pack member decoder enforced a 16 MiB maximum inflated frame, while the common full-reader path currently lacks that bound. Reclaimed the item, still in_progress. Restore the pack limit as pinned-location metadata, enforce it in full/bounded/streamed reads, and verify physical index kind against the decoded frame in every data-returning reader. Add oversized-member and kind-mismatch regressions plus isolated revert proof before final release evidence."
  "2026-10-25T05:36:25.367Z",codex-agent,"Decoded-frame invariant restoration is implemented and validated. PackStorage supplies the original 16 MiB maximum decoded frame with its pinned range; ObjectLocation.validateFrame shares indexed-kind and decoded-size checks across full, bounded and streamed data readers. Bounded reads also enforce exact payload bytes independently of header allowance (limit 8 accepts 8, refuses 9, loose and packed). The new real-tracker regression checks oversized frames and index-kind mismatches through read/readTyped/readIfType/readBoundedTyped/readChunks/readLines/readInventoryObject/pack inventory/state. Native inflater output is observed, so post-decode rejection cannot hide an oversized allocation. Isolated reverts each fail 0/1: removing only the native full-read inflation bound; disabling only shared decoded-frame validation; removing only the exact bounded payload check. Restoring each passes 1/1. The PM-linked regression passes 1/1; the selected related codec/pack/reader target passes 67/67, with stream coverage 100% in all dimensions. Typecheck, test compilation, lint, duplication and docstrings pass. Refreshed final-code public tracker measurement: 330 files, 343 objects, 686 matching reads; 343 loose files / 1,357,191 compressed bytes / 2,187,264 allocated versus 1 pack / 1,262,523 compressed / 1,265,664 allocated. Median/p95 ms are 0.255666/3.250911 loose and 0.266632/1.211096 packed, 301 samples each on a busy shared host; no speed improvement is claimed. Full CI will be rerun for this restoration."
  "2026-10-25T06:14:02.312Z",codex-agent,"Final restored-bound release gate is green for code head ac10c2bef2821807ee5c92c1d57d4be3bd74df5b: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/40166169192 . Node 22 and Node 26 each pass npm run release:check 1,923/1,923 and bun run release:check 1,923/1,923, plus native Bun 32/32 per Node version. All four gates measure 100% statements, branches, functions and lines across all 84 production files, with zero failed, skipped or cancelled suite tests. Windows shipped CLI gc --apply passes on both Node versions and CodeQL passes. This includes the 16 MiB native decoded-pack bound, shared frame kind/size validation, and exact bounded payload limits; the three isolated bound/validation reverts fail and restorations pass as recorded above. Reader matrix remains 25 APIs x 135 write boundaries x live/erased = 6,750 checks, plus 700 resolver schedules; retry bound 8 total attempts. Public fleet tracker copy evidence is docs/indexed-pack-benchmark.json (343 objects, 686 matching comparisons). Self-host regeneration and committed acceptance pass for the code change. Implementation and verification are complete; item remains in_progress for orchestrator review. Releasing the claim and validating the receipt-only final head. No item is closed, no merge or release is performed."
  "2026-10-25T09:18:17.657Z",codex-agent,Round-2 resource-lifetime review reopened implementation work. Reconfirmed the clean pushed branch and existing in_progress item. Investigating synchronous stream worker termination and all object-layer descriptor ownership; adding per-operation descriptor invariants and a low-descriptor-limit soak before exact-head release CI.
  "2026-10-25T09:23:17.585Z",codex-agent,"Resource-lifetime implementation: every explicit object/pack/durability open now registers one idempotent owner in engine/object-files.ts. Resolved locations transfer that owner; synchronous scopes and iterators close in finally. Replaced the worker decoder with pinned pako 3.0.2 synchronous streaming (64-byte compressed pushes, 16 KiB output slots), retaining checksum/frame/hash/denial/pack-bound verification and eliminating deferred decoder handles. The existing writer/resolver matrices remain green: 6,750 writer cells and 700 resolution schedules."
  "2026-10-25T09:23:19.211Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof (resource lifetime): changed only objectPayloadChunks final cleanup from immediate location.close() to queueMicrotask(() => location.close()), restoring deferred closure. Exact command: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"synchronous completed packed streams\" test/object-lifetime.test.ts. Reverted behavior failed 0/1 on operation zero with 23 descriptors versus baseline 22; restored immediate close passed 1/1. No revert retained. The new per-operation invariant has 25 reader APIs x 4 exit modes x 2 representations = 200 cells, with 94 acquired-handle fault/abort injections; scalar early-stop means synchronous completion and empty inventories have no handle to fault. Eight Linux children under ulimit -n 128 each performed 10,000 consecutive synchronous streams without event-loop turns: 80,000 operations, baseline/after 22/22 for every mode and representation, zero EMFILE and zero ownership leaks. Explicit iterator return/throw and Readable.from destroy/AbortController settlement tests also pass."
  "2026-10-25T09:25:33.756Z",codex-agent,"Additional ownership audit found writer-lock fstat was outside its cleanup try. Moved it inside the same synchronous finally as descriptor release and temporary cleanup. Revert proof: restored only the pre-try fstat placement and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"object-layer explicit opens\" test/object-lifetime.test.ts: failed 0/1 (23 descriptors versus 22); restored cleanup scope passed 1/1. An explicit-open guard now prevents object/pack/stream/durability code from bypassing the owner helper. The pm-linked resource suite passed 6/6 before this additional narrow invariant; result recording remains disabled by the existing project policy."
  "2026-10-25T09:28:30.397Z",codex-agent,"Resource-lifetime validation complete: pm test pm-vcs-phase6packs --run --progress --only-last passes the final 7/7 resource cases, including all 80,000 low-limit operations. Targeted c8 command (engine/object-files.ts and engine/object-stream.ts; selected object-lifetime, feature-edges and object-read-protocol cases) passes 12/12 with 100% statements/branches/functions/lines per file, without ignores or threshold changes. Typecheck, build, build:test, lint, duplication and docstring checks pass; committed self-host acceptance passed for implementation commit 9046175. No hosted data or canonical fleet checkout was modified. Existing public tracker measurements remain applicable; the benchmark full-read path retains native zlib. Release CI will validate the final pushed head; PR and final summary carry its URL and counts."
  "2026-10-25T14:13:58.788Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 review: resumed the clean existing branch and in_progress item. Closing byte-level erasure verification for arbitrary object-store files and descriptor-only validation after pinning; earlier reader, durability and resource-lifetime classes remain unchanged. Adding randomized foreign/copy/partial storage cases and unchanged-generation external-retirement interleavings, with isolated revert proofs before exact-head CI."
  "2026-10-25T14:46:51.303Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 implementation: byte-authoritative recursive object-store scanning covers every regular file regardless of name, including foreign pack copies, nested/renamed loose data, partial files, raw/typed frames, payload base64 and embedded zlib members at arbitrary offsets. Private erasure-verification.json stores only length/rolling/SHA-256 fingerprints before denial/deletion, allowing retries after canonical bytes are gone. Foreign files remain owned by their writer; harmless files receive receipt counts/classes and retained copies yield typed class/remedy refusals. No completion is published until the final no-exclusions scan passes. Descriptor validation after pinning now uses fstat/read only; ctime/link count changes from unlink are allowed while in-place size/mtime changes refuse."
  "2026-10-25T14:46:53.091Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 evidence: 120 randomized non-git stores (10 raw/base64/loose/unpack/pack/copy/partial/checksum encodings x 6 locations x retained/clean), including scanner chunk crossings and genuinely compressed payloads without literal raw hits. Pinned reader matrix passed 406 actual boundary injections across the 25 APIs and loose/packed representations; external process retirement leaves generation plus lock inode/mtime unchanged, and erased reads remain denied. Crash tests passed 9 logical proof/scan/publication cuts and 66 native before/after proof/denial write cuts, each SIGKILL followed by convergence with one proof and one receipt. All 9 logical boundaries reject a real competing process on the same tracker; retry then truthfully reports the peer success. Scanner targeted coverage is 100/100/100/100; source inventory is now 85 with unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-25T14:46:54.762Z",codex-agent,"Revert proofs: (1) disabled only scanErasureStorage, restoring inventory-only erasure; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"copied foreign backup.pack\" test/erasure-storage.test.ts failed 0/1 (missing expected refusal while backup remains), restored passed 1/1. (2) restored only readInventoryLocation from the prior pushed head; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"pinned inventory survives external unpack\" test/object-read-protocol.test.ts failed 0/1 with ENOENT lstat of retired pack despite retained fd and unchanged generation/lock, restored passed 1/1. (3) removed only completed-operation de-duplication; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"post-deletion foreign copy leaves\" test/erasure-storage.test.ts failed 0/1 with two receipts instead of one, restored passed 1/1. No revert remains."
  "2026-10-25T14:52:36.498Z",codex-agent,"Compatibility boundary: ErasureDenial currently transports tombstone IDs/digests but not local erasure-verification.json fingerprints. Missing historical/imported evidence now refuses a fresh physical certificate with a restore-evidence remedy; logical denials remain enforced. Follow-up pm-vcs-erasureprooftransport tracks automatic capability-negotiated evidence transfer without erased bytes or tombstone identity changes. Guard revert proof: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"missing historic/imported proof\" test/erasure-storage.test.ts passes 1/1, removing only the missing-evidence guard fails 0/1 with a false-success return while foreign bytes remain, restored passes 1/1."
  "2026-10-25T15:01:11.445Z",codex-agent,"Additional compressed-slice coverage: retain signatures of native DEFLATE member bodies for levels 1/6/9, so removing zlib headers/checksums from a copied chunk does not evade verification. The property corpus is now 144 stores (12 representations x 6 locations x retained/clean), mixing compressible and incompressible payloads. Short sequences use SHA-only matching rather than persisting an invertible short polynomial. Exact revert proof: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"headerless native compressed\" test/erasure-storage.test.ts passes 1/1; removing only native-body signature generation fails 0/1 with false success; restored passes 1/1. Scanner scoped coverage remains 100/100/100/100 over 8 focused cases. Implementation checkpoint d51747b passed committed self-host acceptance."
  "2026-10-25T15:08:02.910Z",codex-agent,"The byte proof also includes dormant objects directories under every registered instance control root, not just the active shared backend. A copied private-instance pack blocks certification; clean private-instance caches remain and contribute to receipt counts. Revert proof: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"dormant object directories\" test/erasure-storage.test.ts passes 1/1; restricting only scanStorage roots to the active backend fails 0/1 (missing retained-copy refusal); restored passes 1/1. Final targeted safety checks cover pre-pin directory substitution, in-place same-size mutation, generic embedded compressed data without native signatures, headerless native members, and missing-evidence restoration."
  "2026-10-25T15:14:54.010Z",codex-agent,"Final local validation: PM-linked node --test test/erasure-storage.test.ts passed 13/13 with the 144-store corpus, 9 logical SIGKILL cuts, 66 native proof/denial cuts and 9 same-tracker peer interleavings. Descriptor matrix passed 406 actual injections; focused namespace/byte-mutation compatibility checks passed 8/8 and final safety checks passed. Scanner coverage passed 9/9 focused cases at 100/100/100/100. Typecheck, test compilation, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication checks pass without threshold changes. Dormant instance records are all preserved and reported as foreign, including native-looking names. Follow-up pm-vcs-erasureprooftransport remains open; primary implementation remains in_progress. Final exact-head release CI will be linked in the PR and handoff."
  "2026-10-25T15:25:41.138Z",codex-agent,"Final adversarial audit found and reproduced a type-independent stripped-wrapper gap in the prior checkpoint: a record-framed body of the same blob payload remained recoverable after false success. Extended signatures across all nine OBJECT_TYPES and native compression levels 1/6/9. The randomized corpus is now 168 stores (14 representations x 6 locations x retained/clean), plus an explicit 27-cell kind/level matrix. Exact revert proof: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"type-independent erasure catches\" test/erasure-storage.test.ts passes 1/1; restricting only native-body generation to the original object kind fails 0/1 (false success); restored passes 1/1. Superseded CI run 40206237312 was cancelled; only the final replacement head will count as release evidence."
  "2026-10-25T16:06:04.172Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 adversarial codec audit: erased payload policy is independent of frame kind. Added signatures for all 9 native frame kinds at levels 1, 6 and 9, plus a bounded recursive zlib/base64 inspection protocol that handles compressed bodies, bundle encodings, arbitrary offsets, alphabetic prefixes, truncated checksums and nested representations. The property extension passes 72 nested cases (9 forms x 4 alignments x 2 offsets), each followed by a clean successful retry. Unsupported inspection depth or resource limits refuse certification. The private fingerprint journal now has an explicit version and checksum; reverting only checksum validation makes the corrupted-journal regression falsely certify a retained copy (0/1), restored validation passes 1/1."
  "2026-10-25T16:08:14.795Z",codex-agent,"Recursive-codec revert proof: disabling only the base64 inspection transition makes the nested native-encoding regression fail 0/1 with Missing expected exception on the first recoverable stripped-body copy; restoring the transition passes 1/1, including all 72 offset/alignment cases and their successful clean retries. Scanner descriptor ownership returns to baseline on injected mid-stream failure; native zlib contexts are closed synchronously on all exits."
