  "2026-10-25T16:42:37.575Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40211196912 exposed two compatibility regressions on the first round-3 head: zero-byte erasure incorrectly broadened to unrelated empty structural kinds; the existing 32 MiB streaming-erasure child exceeded its unchanged 30-second timeout. Fixed zero-byte scope to its actual typed identity and replaced per-pattern-length rolling work with one bounded eight-byte suffix filter plus full SHA-256 confirmation. No timeout, memory budget or coverage threshold was raised. The two existing regressions now pass 2/2 locally: corpus elapsed 7.4 seconds, retained array buffers 1,179,665 bytes at the same boundary (budget 8 MiB). Removed a redundant second-pass content check: both independent physical scans and verified identity/path passes remain. Adding meaningful coverage for strict inventory refusals and suffix collisions before rerunning the exact-head gates."
